@description REAPER MCP — Model Context Protocol interface (immersive/spatial audio)
@version 1.10.0
@author James Livingston
@provides
  [darwin] reaper_mcp.dylib https://github.com/inseglet-audio/inseglet/releases/download/v$version/reaper_mcp.dylib
@changelog
  Correctness release: our BS.1770-4 RLB filter was non-conformant, and every loudness figure
  Inseglet has ever reported read LOW by a constant. Surface UNCHANGED (190 tools /
  3 resources / 5 prompts) - no new verbs, no new parameters.
  *** THIS BREAKS NUMERIC COMPARABILITY WITH v1.9.0 AND EARLIER for ABSOLUTE loudness. ***
  Figures reported by any prior release are low by 0.047099 / 0.043277 / 0.023566 / 0.021652 LU
  at 44.1 / 48 / 88.2 / 96 kHz. RELATIVE quantities - channel balances, deltas, ratios, LRA,
  activity fractions - are unaffected, because the correction is a pure gain at every frequency
  and the shift cancels. Add the constant for your sample rate to compare archived absolute
  figures against v1.10.0 output.
  The K-weighting stage-2 (RLB) highpass divided its numerator by a0, forcing the passband gain
  to exactly 1.000000000000. BS.1770-4 Table 1 keeps that numerator as exactly [1, -2, 1] - it
  is not normalised - and its gain is a0 = 1.004994898715 at 48 kHz. The -0.691 calibration
  term is defined against the TABULATED filter, so the normalised form read low by the constant
  above at every frequency. Moved by the fix: analysis.meter's channelsDetail[].kLevelLkfs,
  accessor_meter, object_loudness, stem_loudness, dialog_loudness, downmix_loudness,
  gatedLoudness() and the intent sidecar's expectLufs claims.
  The K-weighting shelf gain constant was also truncated to 12 significant digits where the
  reference carries 16, reaching b1 as a 1.044942e-12 error against Table 1. Worth about
  3.3e-12 LU - below every measurement - but it was the whole of a discrepancy that had been
  attributed to the table's own precision rather than to us.
  Verified live against a running REAPER on 28 windows: the shift reproduced to 3.5e-12 LU and
  the cross-engine residual column came back invariant to 3.5e-12 LU. Cross-checked against a
  second independent BS.1770-4 implementation on 13 rows: the two now agree to 1.7799e-12 LU,
  where before the fix they differed by exactly the constant above - with Inseglet on the low
  side and the other implementation conformant.
  unit.meter now gates all five coefficients of BOTH filter stages against Table 1 at 1e-12,
  with a negative control that rejects the pre-fix numerator. The previous check gated the
  K-curve against flatness at 1 kHz to +/- 1.2 dB, which is 28x too loose to see a 0.043 dB
  error.
